From b2a273948809bce19b4fb94f85817ac7ccbabb8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:29:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: default input bindings follow PCSX2 (keyboard) and
 XInput (Xbox gamepad)

Patch 0038's defaults copied the runner's old hard-coded mapping. They now
follow the common standard:

- Keyboard = PCSX2 v2.9.134's default keyboard mapping
  (pcsx2/Input/InputManager.cpp GetKeyboardGenericBindingMapping): arrows =
  d-pad, W/S/A/D = left stick, T/G/F/H = right stick, K/L/J/I = cross/circle/
  square/triangle, Q/E = L1/R1, 1/3 = L2/R2, 2/4 = L3/R3, ENTER = start,
  BACKSPACE = select. Nothing else (the old X/SPACE, C/ESCAPE, Z/KP_0, V/KP_1,
  LEFT/RIGHT_SHIFT, TAB defaults are gone).
- Gamepad 0 = PCSX2's XInput mapping (pcsx2/Input/XInputSource.cpp) in
  raylib's names, as before, except L2/R2: raylib 5.5 on desktop reports LT/RT
  as axes (-1 released .. 1 pulled) and sets LEFT/RIGHT_TRIGGER_2 only past
  0.1 (55% travel). l2/r2 now list the button and the trigger axis; a button
  list in [gamepad] may name LEFT_TRIGGER / RIGHT_TRIGGER (code
  kTriggerAxisCode + axis), down above trigger_threshold of travel.
- Dead zones = Xinput.h XINPUT_GAMEPAD_LEFT/RIGHT_THUMB_DEADZONE (7849, 8689
  of 32767), trigger threshold XINPUT_GAMEPAD_TRIGGER_THRESHOLD (30 of 255).
  ini: deadzone sets both sticks; deadzone_left / deadzone_right override it
  wherever they are in the file; trigger_threshold.
- Keyboard and gamepad both live (as in PCSX2): a button is down if either
  source has it down; a stick is the gamepad's after its dead zone, or the
  keyboard's when the gamepad stick is inside it. Replaces "gamepad present =
  keyboard ignored".
- InputSource gains gamepadTriggerTravel (raylib: raylibTriggerTravel, GLFW
  -1..1 to 0..1; Android 0..1 as is); applyDeadzone is public.

Tests: the defaults table equals the spec entry by entry (16 keys, 8 stick
keys, 16 gamepad buttons + 2 trigger axes, axes, device, dead zones,
threshold) and by behaviour; old default keys unbound; per-stick dead zones
and trigger threshold, raylib trigger travel, ini overrides independent of
order; keyboard and gamepad merge; bad lines for the new entries. Against
0038's implementation: 496/502 (all 6 input cases fail).
