-// the mapping PSPadBackend had hard-coded (gamepad 0 when present, else the keyboard; no dead zone).
+// start-up from input.ini (PS2X_INPUT_INI=<path> overrides <exe dir>/input.ini); no file = the defaults:
+//   keyboard = PCSX2's default keyboard mapping (pcsx2/Input/InputManager.cpp, GetKeyboardGenericBindingMapping):
+//     arrows = d-pad, WASD = left stick, TFGH = right stick, K/L/J/I = cross/circle/square/triangle,
+//     Q/E = L1/R1, 1/3 = L2/R2, 2/4 = L3/R3, ENTER = start, BACKSPACE = select;
+//   gamepad 0 = PCSX2's XInput mapping (pcsx2/Input/XInputSource.cpp): A/B/X/Y = cross/circle/square/triangle,
+//     LB/RB = L1/R1, LT/RT = L2/R2, stick clicks = L3/R3, Back/Start = select/start, sticks = sticks;
+//   dead zones = Xinput.h's XINPUT_GAMEPAD_LEFT/RIGHT_THUMB_DEADZONE (7849, 8689 of 32767) and trigger press
+//     threshold XINPUT_GAMEPAD_TRIGGER_THRESHOLD (30 of 255).
+// Keyboard and gamepad are both live: a button is down when either has it down; a stick is the gamepad's unless
+// it is inside its dead zone, then the keyboard's.
 //
 // input.ini (case-insensitive names; ';' or '#' starts a comment; several codes per button comma-separated):
-//   [keyboard]                     raylib key names without KEY_: X, ENTER, RIGHT_SHIFT, KP_0, ...
-//   cross = X, SPACE
-//   stick_left = W, S, A, D        four keys: up, down, left, right (default: none)
+//   [keyboard]                     raylib key names without KEY_: K, ENTER, BACKSPACE, ONE, ...
